# Folder macronode Description sync

## Creation path (source of truth)

1. Left panel → expand a **folder** box
2. Click **Create a new Document** (sets `parentDocId`)
3. User writes title + body in the macronode → Save
4. `syncNodeToParentDoc` inserts/updates a linked H1 title inside the parent folder with `hideColorLink: true`

This must work for **every** new document with a parent folder — not a one-off title.

## Where Description appears

| Surface | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Left panel folder expand | **Title only** (File icon + title) |
| Open folder body | Under each **linked** macronode title (H1/TODO): `Description: {excerpt} continue reading` (+ Completed if on) |

## Color node link (query handle)

| Origin | Color handle |
|---|---|
| **Create a new Document** (left panel) | **Hidden** (`hideColorLink`) — `continue reading` opens the doc |
| Link created **inside the open folder** (Create node + color) | **Shown** as today |

## Delete rules

1. **Delete from left panel expand** → purge node entity **and** title/Description/blocks from the parent folder (`deleteNode` → `deleteNodeAndDocBlocks`).
2. **Remove layers inside the open folder** (detach / empty-title delete) → strip the linked owner bundle from folder blocks, but **keep** the document under the folder in the left panel (`parentDocId` retained).

## Data

- Excerpt from `node.content` **body** via `getNodeWritingExcerpt` / `getNodeWritingBodyPlainText` (max 120)
- `continue reading` opens that macronode
- `mergeMissingLinkedOwnerBundles` + draft purge when node deleted from panel

## Key files

- `LinkedMacronodeDescription.jsx` — Description line under linked titles
- `DocBlockStack.jsx` — mounts Description; respects `hideColorLink`
- `nodesStore.syncNodeToParentDoc` + `panelSyncedBlockFields`
- `docNodeSync.removeLinkedOwnerBundleFromBlocks` / `mergeMissingLinkedOwnerBundles`
